# Intropy.Topology

A small .NET library providing an **in-memory model and fluent builder** for an
Intropy system topology (systems, their component blocks, infrastructure
resources, and the data-flow edges between them).

## Scope — read this first

`Intropy.Topology` itself is **model + builder only**. It does **not** serialize
or write files. Do **not** reintroduce `System.Text.Json`, `ToJson`/`Save`, or
serialization attributes (`[JsonPropertyName]`, `[JsonStringEnumMemberName]`)
into that project — keeping the model serialization-agnostic is the point.

Serialization lives in the separate `Intropy.Topology.Serialization` project,
which is the **one** sanctioned exception: it emits the
`topology.intropy.io/v1` record the Go deployment tooling decodes. It writes no
files either — it produces the JSON text; the host decides where it goes.

The division of responsibility with the CLI is deliberate and load-bearing:

- **This repo owns structure** — components, wiring, Dapr `scopes`, connector
  names and the bindings they materialize as, workload shape (CronJob vs
  Deployment), schedules, app ports, and validation.
- **The CLI owns environment values** — namespace, registry/image repository,
  platform namespace, OTLP endpoint, per-environment pub/sub backend and secret
  name, `DOTNET_ENVIRONMENT`, kustomize rendering, digest pinning and promotion.
- **Neither owns secrets.** No address, host, URL, or credential belongs in this
  model. Staging and prod share a connector's transport *kind* and differ only in
  configuration, which is why one declaration covers every deployed environment.

## Layout

- `src/Intropy.Topology/` — the library (`net10.0`)
  - `Models/` — plain data types: `SystemTopology` (root), `Component`,
    `Resource`, `Transport`, `Edge`, `Trigger`, `Generator`, and the
    `ComponentType` / `ResourceType` / `EdgeKind` / `TriggerKind` /
    `WorkloadKind` enums. `Ref` (internal) builds the `component:<name>` /
    `resource:<name>` reference strings edges use.
  - `Building/` — `SystemBuilder` (entry point) and `ComponentBuilder` (fluent
    per-component wiring).
- `src/Intropy.Topology.Serialization/` — `TopologyRecord.ToJson`/`Write`, the
  `topology.intropy.io/v1` emitter, plus the internal wire DTOs.
- `tests/Intropy.Topology.Tests/`, `tests/Intropy.Topology.Serialization.Tests/`
  — xUnit tests. The serialization tests assert against a checked-in snapshot at
  `Snapshots/order-flow.json`.
- `Intropy.Topology.slnx` — the solution.

## Build & test

```sh
dotnet build Intropy.Topology.slnx
dotnet test Intropy.Topology.slnx
```

The library sets `TreatWarningsAsErrors=true` and `GenerateDocumentationFile=true`,
so warnings (including missing XML doc comments on public members) fail the
build. Public types and members get `///` summaries.

